---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About this site · Path to Integration"
  description="How this site works: build-time content from the repository's Markdown, browser-only progress storage, and the public-safe rule."
>
  <h1>About this site</h1>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>No accounts, no tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a static bundle. There is no backend, no analytics, no cookies and
      no third-party scripts. Nothing you do here is sent anywhere.
    </p>
    <h2>Where your progress lives</h2>
    <p>
      Every checkbox and quiz answer is stored only in your browser's
      <code>localStorage</code>, keyed by stable content IDs derived from the source
      text. Clearing your browser data for this site erases your progress. A later
      phase adds export/import (JSON and Markdown) so you can back up or move it.
    </p>
    <h2>The content is the repository</h2>
    <p>
      The checklist, reading guide, podcast blocks, whitepaper, glossary, labs and
      templates are parsed from this repo's Markdown at build time — the site never
      rewrites or duplicates that content by hand. If a source file changes shape in
      a way the parsers don't expect, the build fails instead of silently dropping
      content.
    </p>
    <h2>The public-safe rule</h2>
    <p>
      This repository is public and deliberately contains no employer-internal
      information: no internal code, architecture, metrics, customer data, call
      recordings, or names of internal systems. The site adds no new sources; public
      vendor pages and documents linked from the repo's reading guide are attributed
      there. If anything here looks like internal material, it shouldn't be — flag it.
    </p>
    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The site targets WCAG 2.1 AA: keyboard navigation, visible focus, semantic
      landmarks, alt text on all art, and a <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> path
      that removes animation. If something is hard to use with a keyboard or a screen
      reader, that's a bug.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s6); }
  .card { padding: var(--s6); }
  .card h2 { margin-top: var(--s6); font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .card h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
